{
  "_comment": [
    "ECS task definition for rithm-api-migrations — the one-off Fargate task",
    "deploy-api.yml runs BEFORE it swaps the service. Replace <ACCOUNT>,",
    "<SECRET_RDS_ADMIN_ARN> and <SHA> before registering.",
    "",
    "Register this by hand once. It is bootstrap documentation, not a deploy",
    "source: deploy-api.yml describes the LIVE definition and patches only the",
    "image, so anything tuned in the console survives every deploy.",
    "",
    "FOUR THINGS THAT WILL BITE:",
    "",
    "1. The secret is the RDS *ADMIN* secret, not the module secret. Migrations",
    "   run as rithm_admin (rithm_master on RDS). The per-module roles hold DML",
    "   privileges only — they have no CREATE on their own schemas — so a",
    "   migration run as rithm_generation fails with a permission error that",
    "   reads like a connection problem.",
    "",
    "2. Every secret ARN needs the TRAILING '::'. The syntax is",
    "   <arn>:<json-key>:<version-stage>:<version-id>; omit the two empty",
    "   trailing fields and ECS injects the entire JSON blob as the value.",
    "",
    "3. assignPublicIp=ENABLED is a run-task PARAMETER, not a task-definition",
    "   field, so it lives in the workflow rather than here — do not go looking",
    "   for it in this file. It is mandatory: there is no NAT gateway, so",
    "   without it the task cannot reach Secrets Manager or RDS.",
    "",
    "4. identity migrates FIRST — it owns the shared public.touch_updated_at",
    "   preamble the other four schemas depend on. run-migrations.sh already",
    "   sequences this. Do not reorder its MODULES array.",
    "",
    "All five DSNs deliberately point at the SAME admin connection: each module",
    "keeps its own alembic_version table inside its own schema, so one",
    "privileged connection applies all five correctly."
  ],
  "family": "rithm-api-migrations",
  "networkMode": "awsvpc",
  "requiresCompatibilities": ["FARGATE"],
  "cpu": "512",
  "memory": "1024",
  "executionRoleArn": "arn:aws:iam::<ACCOUNT>:role/ecsTaskExecutionRole",
  "taskRoleArn": "arn:aws:iam::<ACCOUNT>:role/rithm-api-task-role",
  "containerDefinitions": [
    {
      "name": "migrations",
      "image": "<ACCOUNT>.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/rithm/api:<SHA>",
      "essential": true,
      "command": ["bash", "ops/scripts/run-migrations.sh"],
      "environment": [
        { "name": "ENVIRONMENT", "value": "prod" },
        { "name": "DB_REQUIRE_SSL", "value": "true" },
        { "name": "LOG_LEVEL", "value": "INFO" },
        { "name": "AWS_REGION", "value": "us-east-1" },
        {
          "_note": "Settings has no defaults for these three and refuses to construct without them. Nothing in a migration touches AWS, so the values only need to be well-formed.",
          "name": "ASSETS_BUCKET",
          "value": "<ASSETS_BUCKET>"
        },
        { "name": "SQS_JOBS_QUEUE_URL", "value": "<JOBS_QUEUE_URL>" },
        { "name": "SNS_COMPLETIONS_TOPIC_ARN", "value": "<TOPIC_ARN>" }
      ],
      "secrets": [
        {
          "name": "DB_IDENTITY_DSN",
          "valueFrom": "<SECRET_RDS_ADMIN_ARN>:admin_dsn::"
        },
        {
          "name": "DB_CATALOG_DSN",
          "valueFrom": "<SECRET_RDS_ADMIN_ARN>:admin_dsn::"
        },
        {
          "name": "DB_GENERATION_DSN",
          "valueFrom": "<SECRET_RDS_ADMIN_ARN>:admin_dsn::"
        },
        {
          "name": "DB_CONVERSATION_DSN",
          "valueFrom": "<SECRET_RDS_ADMIN_ARN>:admin_dsn::"
        },
        {
          "name": "DB_PERSONALIZATION_DSN",
          "valueFrom": "<SECRET_RDS_ADMIN_ARN>:admin_dsn::"
        }
      ],
      "logConfiguration": {
        "logDriver": "awslogs",
        "options": {
          "awslogs-group": "/ecs/rithm-api-migrations",
          "awslogs-region": "us-east-1",
          "awslogs-stream-prefix": "migrations",
          "awslogs-create-group": "true"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
